Comments: [Evaluator: Christian Iliadis; Date: 01/15/2024]
1. C2S values for Ex = 0 to 1373 keV for the 28Al mirror levels are adopted from Endt 1977. Those for 28Al levels at Ex = 1620 to 3542 keV are averages of the
   values compiled in Endt and van der Leun 1978. We disregarded the values reported by Maher et al., PRC 5, 1313 (1972) since they exceed other measured results
   and shell-model values by a factor >2.
2. 28Al - 28P mirror assignments are adopted from Endt 1998 and Iliadis et al. 1999. 
3. Uncertainties on some proton widths have been increased over nominal values when transfers were mixed with a dominant higher orbital angular momentum transfer
   component, or when the agreement between measurements was poor.
4. As mentioned in Iliadis et al. 1999, the C2S values for the 28Al mirror levels at Ex = 2201 and 2272 keV listed in column 5 of Tab. 28.13 in Endt and van der 
   Leun 1978 have to be multiplied by a factor of 6.
5. The gamma-ray partial widths of the 28Al mirror levels at Ex = 3011 and 3542 keV have not been measured and we adopt the shell-model values of Endt and Booten
   1993; these correspond to Er = 806 and 1461 keV, respectively.
6. For Er = 845 keV, only the resonance strength can be estimated (given by the gamma-ray partial width) because the ell = 0 component of C2S has not been measured.
